Henry Ederle, played by Kim Bodnia.

9
00:50:28,695 --> 00:50:34,695
Gertrude Ederle, played by Jeanette Hain.

10
00:56:05,217 --> 00:56:11,217
James Sullivan, played by Glenn Fleshler.

11
01:01:41,739 --> 01:01:47,739
Young Woman and the Sea is a 2024 American biographical sports film directed by Joachim
Rønning and written by Jeff Nathanson, based on the 2009 book by Glenn Stout.

12
01:07:18,260 --> 01:07:24,260
Produced by Walt Disney Pictures and Jerry Bruckheimer Films, the film stars Daisy Ridley as Gertrude Ederle,
an American competitive swimmer who became the first woman to swim across the English Channel.

13
01:12:54,782 --> 01:13:00,782
It also stars Tilda Cobham-Hervey, Stephen Graham, Kim Bodnia,
Christopher Eccleston, and Glenn Fleshler in supporting roles.

14
01:18:31,304 --> 01:18:37,304
Development on the film began in 2015 after producer Jerry Bruckheimer acquired the film rights to the book, and established a
distribution deal with Paramount Pictures, with Nathanson attached to write it and Lily James cast as Ederle.

15
01:24:07,826 --> 01:24:13,826
Paramount eventually put the project in turnaround.

16
01:29:44,347 --> 01:29:50,347
In 2020, Walt Disney Pictures acquired the project with Ridley
set to portray Ederle and Rønning to direct it.

17
01:35:20,869 --> 01:35:26,869
Principal photography took place between May and June 2022.

18
01:40:57,391 --> 01:41:03,391
Young Woman and the Sea premiered at the Hollywood
Roosevelt Hotel in Los Angeles on May 16, 2024.

19
01:46:33,913 --> 01:46:39,913
Originally set for release by Disney on its streaming service Disney+, the film had a limited
theatrical release after positive test screenings in the United States on May 31, 2024.

20
01:52:10,434 --> 01:52:16,434
It received positive reviews from critics.

21
01:57:46,956 --> 01:57:52,956
The film explores themes of english channel, biography,
based on true story, swimming, 1920s.

22
02:03:23,478 --> 02:03:29,478
The tone is emotional.
